}

vars:pre-request {
  adminEmail: admin@aip.com
  adminPassword: admin
  locale: en
  legalPageKey: 1
}

docs {
# Rose API Collection

Use the `Local` environment for application requests. Its `baseUrl` already includes `/api`, so application URLs begin with `/app`.

## App request sequences

Customer registration is: **Register Request OTP** → **Register Verify OTP** → **Register Update Location**. Each response replaces `customerSessionToken`; the final step captures `customerAccessToken`. For an existing customer, use **Login Request OTP** → **Login Verify OTP** instead. **Resend OTP** is valid only while the current customer session represents the register or login OTP flow.

Provider registration is: **Get Categories** → **Register Request OTP** → **Register Verify OTP** → **Register Upload Documents**. Set `specialtyId` in the Local environment to an active category before registration; registration requires at least one unique, active category, a display image, National ID front and back images, and a selfie-verification image. The National ID request fields use `nationalId[]`, with front first and back second. Registration ends in pending status and does not issue a bearer token. For an active provider, use **Login Request OTP** → **Login Verify OTP**; the successful login captures `providerAccessToken`. **Resend OTP** is valid only while a provider register or login OTP session is active.

An active KYC-approved provider can add portfolio images one at a time using **Add Portfolio Photo**. Use **List Portfolio Photos** to retrieve paginated images and capture a `portfolioPhotoId`, which **Delete Portfolio Photo** uses to remove that image.

An active KYC-approved provider can submit one Saudi payout account using **Add Bank Details**, then use **Get Bank Details** to retrieve its bank name and masked IBAN. Account details cannot be edited or replaced through the API.

An active KYC-approved provider can submit a named image with **Upload Document**. **Get Documents** returns custom uploads together with the National ID front/back images and selfie verification captured during registration. Custom document names must be unique per provider.

Providers use **Toggle Availability Status** to switch their marketplace availability on or off. Switching online requires at least one active service and a saved availability schedule with an enabled day; otherwise the API returns 422. Offline providers are hidden from the marketplace and cannot receive bookings.

All OTP examples use `123456`, which the local API accepts for development. Request/response scripts keep customer and provider session, OTP, and bearer-token variables separate.

The Local environment uses currently seeded category, service, service-area, and replyable-review IDs. Replace an ID if your local database has been reseeded.

Customer review creation requires a bearer token and a completed booking owned by that customer which has not already been reviewed. Booking list and detail responses include `review.canCreate`; show the Rate & Review action only when it is `true`. A submitted review is returned in the same field. Provider replies require a bearer token for the provider who owns that review and can be submitted only once.

Customer booking creation is: **List Providers** → **Get Provider** → **Get Available Slots** → either **Create Booking - Saved Address** or **Create Booking - Map Pin** → **Get Booking Details**. Copy a marketplace-ready provider ID into the editable `providerId` Local-environment variable, then copy one of that provider's active service IDs into the editable `serviceId` variable. Run **Get Provider** to capture a matching same-category `secondServiceId` for that `serviceId`. The slots request captures the first two available timestamps for their combined duration. If `secondServiceId` remains empty, configure another active service in the first service's category before running the multi-service examples. For saved-address booking, run **List Addresses** or **Create Address** first so `addressId` is populated. Set `bookingDate` to a future enabled availability date before fetching slots. The two create requests are alternatives; when both are run, they use different captured slots. Customers can withdraw pending requests at any time and cancel accepted upcoming bookings before the configured cancellation window through **Cancel Booking**; its reason is `customer_request` or `other`, and comments are optional.

**Get Provider** includes an active-review `reviews` section. It contains the reviewer's name and image, rating, review text, and creation date, with pagination metadata. Use optional `reviewsPage` and `reviewsPageSize` query parameters (defaults: `1` and `10`) to load further reviews.

New booking requests contain no payment data. They start with booking `status` and request `requestStatus` set to `pending`; the details endpoint includes `requestExpiresAt` and `remainingSeconds`. If the provider does not respond before the configured timeout, subsequent details responses show `status: cancelled` and `requestStatus: expired`.

## Telr Hosted Payment Page

The `telr-hosted-payment-page` folder demonstrates Telr's redirect checkout flow without storing or sending card details through Rose. Select the **Telr Sandbox** environment, enter the Store ID and Authentication Key supplied by Telr, and use a unique `telrCartId` for every create-session attempt.

Run **1. Create payment session** from your server after creating a Rose booking/order. It saves Telr's `order.ref` and `order.url`. Redirect the shopper's browser to `telrPaymentUrl` immediately; do not mark the Rose order as paid based only on the browser return URL. After Telr redirects to the authorised, declined, or cancelled URL, run **2. Check payment status** (or have the backend run the same request) and use the returned payment status to update your local order.

The collection uses `test: "1"`, which keeps the example in Telr test mode. Change it only after Telr has enabled and configured the live account. Credentials are intentionally environment variables and must never be committed.

Provider booking management is: **Get All Booking Requests** → **Get Booking Details** → **Update Booking Request Status** → **Get All Bookings** → **Start Upcoming Booking**. The requests call captures the first pending `bookingId`. Set `providerBookingRequestStatus` to `accepted` or `rejected` before updating it. Accepted requests become `upcoming`; rejected requests become `cancelled`. Only accepted upcoming bookings can be started, changing their status to `in_progress`. The provider bookings list accepts `upcoming`, `in_progress`, or `completed` as `providerBookingListStatus`.

Providers can cancel only their own upcoming bookings through **Cancel Booking**. The request requires one of: `personal_emergency`, `health_issue`, `equipment_or_supply_issue`, `scheduling_conflict`, `unable_to_reach_location`, or `other`; `comments` are optional. Booking responses include `canCancel` for showing the cancellation action.

Accepted upcoming and in-progress bookings support private customer/provider chat. REST requests cover history, text, one JPG/PNG/WebP image up to 5 MB with optional caption, read-through receipts, and authenticated image download. Booking responses expose `chat.canAccess`, `chat.canSend`, and `chat.unreadCount`; booking details also expose counterpart presence. Socket.IO uses namespace `/chat`, handshake auth `{ token, role }`, and emits `chat:message`, `chat:read`, and `chat:presence`. Closed bookings keep read-only history.

## Current app enums

| Field | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `locale` | `en`, `ar` |
| customer `gender` | `1` male, `2` female, `3` other |
| service `gender` | `0` both, `1` men, `2` women |
| legal `pageKey` (customer) | `1` terms, `2` privacy, `3` cookie |
| legal `pageKey` (provider) | customer values plus `4` provider agreement |
| provider explore `sortBy` | `1` topRated, `2` nearest, `3` lowestPrice, `4` mostReviewed |
| availability `bufferMinutes` | `15`, `30`, `45`, `60` |
| customer address `label` | `1` home, `2` work, `3` other |
| booking `status` | `pending`, `upcoming`, `in_progress`, `completed`, `cancelled` |
| booking `requestStatus` | `pending`, `accepted`, `rejected`, `expired` |

Availability updates must include each of `monday` through `sunday` exactly once. Times use 24-hour `HH:mm`; enabled days require a start and end time with the end later than the start, while disabled days may use `null` times.
}
